BEYOND-REF side check, 16 Nov 2026 (sympy, inline command, no script file).
Claim [P]: u = tanh^(l+1)(rho/2) > 0 solves h^2 u = (l+1) N u, N = 1/(1+cosh rho).
Hand proof (r = tanh(rho/2), d/drho = N d/dr, N' = -r, sinh rho = r/N):
  u'' = (l+1) N [ -r^(l+1) + l N r^(l-1) ],  lambda^2 u / sinh^2 = l(l+1) N^2 r^(l-1),
  so -u'' + lambda^2 u/sinh^2 = (l+1) N r^(l+1) = (l+1) N u.
Consequence (ground-state representation): <v,(h^2 - (l+1)N) v> = int u^2 |(v/u)'|^2 >= 0 on the form domain,
  hence N <= h^2/(l+1), i.e. C_l = 1/(l+1) exactly-bounded for every l (the lane's "observation, not proved").
Symbolic residual -u'' + l(l+1)u/sinh^2 - (l+1)Nu evaluated at (rho, l) = (0.7, 2), (2.3, 5), (5.1, 17), 30 digits:
